   "html_text": "Since the axiom ⟦M⟧ implies the AC and the CH, any model of the negation of the AC or the CH must violate ⟦M⟧ . So, let’s illustrate the idea of forcing in the case of building a model for the negation of ⟦M⟧ . We start with a transitive model ⟦M⟧ of ZFC, which we may assume, without loss of generality, to be a model of ⟦M⟧ . To violate ⟦M⟧ we need to expand ⟦M⟧ by adding a new set ⟦M⟧ so that, in the expanded model, ⟦M⟧ will be non-constructible. Since all hereditarily-finite sets are construct",
